Frappe Scheduler Critical Bugs: NULL Trap + Timezone Mismatch · Issue #37490 · frappe/frappe · GitHub (https://github.com/frappe/frappe/issues/37490)
citeturn31563search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Screenshot 2: last_execution showing future timestamp 2026-02-07 08:46:06 when current time is 2026-02-06 23:44:00 (Issue Two) ...   * Zero error messages or warnings
    bench --site test.local mariadb -e \
      "SELECT status FROM \`tabEmail Queue\` ORDER BY creation DESC LIMIT 1;"

Before fix: status = "Not Sent" (stuck forever)

After fix: status = "Sent" (processed automatically)

* * *

Screenshots Reference

Screenshot 1: last_execution showing NULL for fresh site (Issue One)

Screenshot 2: last_execution showing future timestamp 2026-02-07 08:46:06 when current time is 2026-02-06 23:44:00 (Issue Two)

Screenshot 3: After bootstrap, last_execution showing correct current timestamp and scheduler working

* * *

Additional Context

Why these bugs are hard to detect:

  * Zero error messages or warnings
  * System diagnostics show "healthy"
  * Requires database inspection to identify
  * Symptoms appear unrelated (emails not sending, reports missing)

Community impact:

  * Multiple forum threads about "scheduler inactive"
  * Many "emails stuck in queue" support requests
  * Users struggle for hours/days before finding workaround
  * Every fresh installation affected

* * *

Deployment Workaround (Until Fixed in Framework)

For production deployments, add to site creation process:

Step 1: Set MariaDB to UTC in /etc/mysql/mariadb.conf.d/50-server.cnf:
    
    [mysqld]
    default-time-zone = '+00:00'

